<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Christos Tsirigotis">
  <section class="anchor" id="about-me" style="margin-bottom: 18px;">
  <h1>About me</h1>
  <div class="about-hero" style="margin: 8px 0 16px;">
    <div>
        I'm <strong>Christos Tsirigotis</strong>, a Ph.D. Candidate in Universit&eacute; de Montr&eacute;al and Mila, the Quebec AI Institute, supervised by Prof. <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=km6CP8cAAAAJ" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Aaron Courville</a>. My current research explores representation learning algorithms for robust out-of-distribution generalization in foundational discriminative models and retrieval systems. In the past, I have worked on deep generative models and over the years, since starting my Ph.D., I have gradually shifted my focus towards systematic generalization and foundational models. My work have been published in NeurIPS, ICML, and ICLR, for which I have been serving as a reviewer for many years. I was a visiting reseracher at ServiceNow Research for 2 years, from 2022-2024. My alma mater is Aristotle University of Thessaloniki, Greece, where I obtained a Diploma in Electrical and Computer Engineering (integrated B.Sc + M.Sc) with distinctions. During my studies there I focused on autonomous systems and robotics, while I had the opportunity to be involved for 2 years in Pandora Robotics, developing full-stack autonomous UGV pipelines from perception and data fusion to planning and control.
    </div>
    <picture>
      <source srcset="/images/christos.avif" type="image/avif" />
      <img src="/images/christos_320.png"
           alt="Portrait of Christos Tsirigotis"
           width="320" height="320"
           loading="eager"
           decoding="async"
           class="portrait portrait--hero" />
    </picture>
  </div>
  <p>
  Research topics that I am particularly interested at the moment include:
    <ul>
      <li>Out-of-distribution generalization and robustness in machine learning models</li>
      <li>Improving capabilities of multi-modal foundational models: spatial understanding and grounding, more robust fusion and visual instruction training methods.</li>
      <li>Retrieval-augmented models and retrieval systems</li>
      <li>Probabilistic modeling, deep generative models and sampling: parallel sampling, guided sampling, diverse sampling.</li>
      <li>Exploration and open-endedness</li>
    </ul>
  </p>
  <p>
  Interested in discussing potential collaborations, research ideas, or just want to say hi? Feel free to reach out through any of the social links below!
  </p>

